  "<section class=\"course-page\" id=\"lesson-01\" data-chapter11-complete=\"overview\" hidden=\"\">\n<div class=\"p2-topic\">\n<header class=\"page-header\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-23\">Learn · Chapter 11</p>\n<h1 data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-24\">Nervous communication</h1>\n<p class=\"lesson-question\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-chapter-25\">How does your body detect a change and respond?</p>\n<div class=\"goal-strip\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-01\">Learning goal</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-02\">I can explain how the nervous system detects changes and directs responses.</p>\n</div>\n<div>\n<p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-03\">Before you begin</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-04\">Start here: a stimulus is a change; a response is what the body does after that change.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<details class=\"page-guide\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-summary\"><strong>How to complete this lesson</strong> — Learn → practise → required check → finish</summary>\n<div>\n<ol>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-01\"><strong>Start with the lesson.</strong> Read the learning goal and “Before you begin,” then work through the explanation, diagrams and examples below. The embedded textbook is optional support: open it when you want another explanation or a closer look at a figure.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-02\"><strong>Use the learning goal and starting reminder.</strong> The learning goal above tells you what you must be able to explain. Read “Before you begin” next to connect this lesson to what you already know.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-03\"><strong>Work through the online lesson in order.</strong> Read each teaching section and study its diagrams, examples and comparisons. Select an underlined biology term when you need its meaning. Use the video or Vocabulary help when an idea is still unclear.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-04\"><strong>Complete the required chapter check.</strong> Open the check near the bottom and select Start. For multiple choice, select Check answer; a correct answer unlocks the related writing. Answer in your own words and select Save written response for every response box.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-05\"><strong>Submit only when the required work is complete.</strong> Check that every required item has been attempted and every written response is saved. Then select Submit and finish. This stops the timer, records the completed run in All My Work and updates chapter progress.</li>\n<li data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-06\"><strong>Use optional practice only when it helps.</strong> Optional source practice and Practice &amp; Review activities can help you study, but they do not count toward the 12 required chapter checks.</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-guide-07\"><strong>Expected work:</strong> complete the lesson and submit the required chapter check. Use optional reading, videos and practice when they help. Drafts save automatically as you work in this browser.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n<div class=\"textbook-band\">\n<div>\n<p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-05\">Optional embedded reading</p>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-06\"><strong>Chapter 11 · pp. 367–371</strong></p>\n</div>\n<a class=\"text-link\" href=\"#textbook-library\" data-book-page=\"8\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-07\">Open at p. 367</a>\n</div>\n<p class=\"lesson-term-strip\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-teacher-voice-terms\"><strong>Key terms:</strong> stimulus · response · receptor · effector · neuron · homeostasis</p>\n<details class=\"lesson-vocabulary-help\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-teacher-voice-vocab-summary\">Vocabulary help</summary>\n<section class=\"lesson-words\" aria-labelledby=\"lesson-01-anchor-words\">\n<p class=\"section-label\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-08\">Key terms</p>\n<h2 id=\"lesson-01-anchor-words\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-09\">Words for this lesson</h2>\n<p data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-10\">Use these definitions when you need help with a term.</p>\n<dl>\n<div>\n<dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"homeostasis\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-11\">homeostasis</button></dt>\n<dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-12\">keeping internal conditions relatively stable</dd>\n</div>\n<div>\n<dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"response\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-13\">response</button></dt>\n<dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-14\">what the body does after a stimulus</dd>\n</div>\n<div>\n<dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"central nervous system\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-15\">central nervous system (CNS)</button></dt>\n<dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-16\">the brain and spinal cord</dd>\n</div>\n<div>\n<dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"peripheral nervous system\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-17\">peripheral nervous system (PNS)</button></dt>\n<dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-18\">nerves connecting the CNS with the rest of the body</dd>\n</div>\n</dl>\n</section>\n<details class=\"lesson-term-inventory\">\n<summary data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-19\">More vocabulary for this lesson</summary>\n<div>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"lesson-01-communication-terms\">\n<h3 id=\"lesson-01-communication-terms\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-20\">Communication and regulation</h3>\n<dl>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-21\">sensory input</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-22\">information about a change inside or outside the body</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-23\">integration</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-24\">processing information and organizing an appropriate response</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-25\">motor output</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-26\">instructions carried to a responding structure</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"effector\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-27\">effector</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-28\">a muscle, gland or other structure that carries out a response</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"response\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-29\">response</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-30\">the resulting change in activity</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-31\">electrochemical message</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-32\">a neural message involving electrical changes and chemical signals</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"hormone\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-33\">hormone</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-34\">a chemical messenger carried through the bloodstream</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"homeostasis\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-35\">homeostasis</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-36\">maintenance of relatively stable internal conditions</dd></div>\n</dl>\n</section>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"lesson-01-system-terms\">\n<h3 id=\"lesson-01-system-terms\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-37\">Systems, cells and structures</h3>\n<dl>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"central nervous system\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-38\">central nervous system (CNS)</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-39\">the brain and spinal cord</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"peripheral nervous system\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-40\">peripheral nervous system (PNS)</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-41\">the nerves connecting the CNS with the rest of the body</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt><button type=\"button\" class=\"bio-term\" data-bio-term=\"neuron\" data-bio-term-route=\"lesson-01\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-42\">neuron</button></dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-43\">a cell specialized to receive, conduct and pass information</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-44\">glial cell</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-45\">a cell that supports, protects and nourishes neurons</dd></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-term-row\"><dt data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-46\">nerve</dt><dd data-canvas-helper-edit-key=\"p3-l01-setup-47\">a bundle of many nerve fibres surrounded by protective tissue</dd></div>\n</dl>\n</section>\n</div>\n</details>\n</details>\n</header>\n",
